# Citation metadata for GENESIS. Renders as "Cite this repository"
# in the GitHub sidebar. After minting the Zenodo DOI, replace the
# placeholder `value:` field below.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GENESIS in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "GENESIS — Multisensor Satellite Analysis Toolbox for ArcGIS Pro"
abstract: >
  GENESIS is an ArcGIS Pro Python Toolbox for remote-sensing analysis of
  Sentinel-2 L2A, Landsat 8/9 Collection 2 Level 2, and ASTER L2 (AST_07XT)
  imagery in a single unified workflow. It provides cloud-masked
  mosaicking with provenance tracking and per-mosaic band-mapping
  sidecars; sensor-aware spectral indices and composites (~25 indices
  + ~8 composites covering vegetation, water, built-up, and
  mineralogical / hydrothermal alteration targets);
  PCA / MNF / ICA statistical transformations with reloadable
  ``.npz`` archives, human-readable ``.txt`` summaries and a
  self-contained HTML dashboard per run; Spectral Angle Mapper
  classification; and per-pixel temporal statistics over a mosaic
  scratch (NDVI moments + persistence, NDWI water occurrence, the
  Lv 2013 GDV ratio and the Eamus/Naumburg dry-season floor — all
  groundwater-dependent-vegetation indicators with published
  precedent). Used to support analytical work for the GENESIS
  Horizon Europe project (genesisnbs.eu, grant agreement Nº 101157447),
  in particular processing satellite imagery over the Faial (Azores)
  demonstrator site — an aquifer storage and recovery study at
  Furo das Cancelas targeting saltwater intrusion mitigation.
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-22"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Gonçalves"
    given-names: "Pedro"
    affiliation: "Laboratório Nacional de Energia e Geologia (LNEG)"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add when known
repository-code: "https://github.com/PedroMMGoncalves/GENESIS"
keywords:
  - "remote sensing"
  - "sentinel-2"
  - "landsat"
  - "aster"
  - "arcgis pro"
  - "python toolbox"
  - "geological mapping"
  - "mineral mapping"
  - "hydrothermal alteration"
  - "cloud masking"
  - "geometric median"
  - "spectral angle mapper"
  - "temporal statistics"
  - "groundwater-dependent vegetation"
  - "phreatophyte mapping"
identifiers:
  # After minting the Zenodo DOI for your first release, paste the
  # concept DOI here (the one that always points to the latest version).
  # Format: 10.5281/zenodo.<numeric_id>
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER"
    description: "Concept DOI (latest release, via Zenodo)"

references:
  - type: website
    title: "GENESIS — Nature-based Solutions for sustainable cities (Horizon Europe project, grant 101157447)"
    url: "https://genesisnbs.eu"
    notes: >
      Parent research context. Funded by the European Union's Horizon
      Europe research and innovation programme under grant agreement
      Nº 101157447. This toolbox is independently authored work used
      in support of GENESIS analytical tasks at the Faial demonstrator
      site. It is not an official project deliverable. Views and
      opinions expressed are those of the author only and do not
      necessarily reflect those of the European Union or CINEA.
  - type: website
    title: "GENESIS — Faial demonstrator site"
    url: "https://genesisnbs.eu/faial/"
    notes: >
      The Faial demonstrator is designing an aquifer storage and
      recovery system at Furo das Cancelas to counter saltwater
      intrusion and re-establish freshwater supply for ~3,000
      inhabitants. This toolbox supports that work by producing
      cloud-removed multisensor mosaics and derived spectral products.
